message: "If you use this code or evidence, please cite it as below."
title: "northwind-cobol-to-go: Northwind IBM i COBOL batch programs NWC620 and NWC700 migrated to Go, with golden-output evidence"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Garrido Tovar"
    given-names: "Eleazar"
license: GPL-3.0-only
repository-code: "https://github.com/RustLangLatam/northwind-cobol-to-go"
date-released: 2026-11-27
version: "1.0.0"
keywords:
  - IBM i
  - AS/400
  - COBOL
  - Db2 for i
  - Go
  - code migration
  - equivalence testing
abstract: >-
  Two batch programs of the public Northwind IBM i COBOL application
  (NWC620, ILE COBOL; NWC700, OPM COBOL/400) migrated to Go gRPC services by
  Milton Prism, with the spooled output of the original programs run on
  PUB400 and the record-by-record comparison: NWC620 168 of 168 records
  identical, NWC700 186 of 188, both in memory and against Db2 for i.
